msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/a5b5bdec-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the making of this lesson, from the extrapolation to the zero-noise case, we get an expectation value of 0.959. Your values might differ. This is substantially better than the raw circuit's expectation value of 0.83, around 13% closer to the ideal value. But you can also see that we are using one data point where the expectation value was down at 0.31. Obviously this data point is of poorer quality. If that data point had been given lower weighting in our linear approximation, and the line were fitted more to the first two data points, we can see the zero-extrapolated estimate would have been higher (nearer the ideal value). This sort of consideration is handled automatically in the ZNE built into Estimator.\n"
msgstr "Saat pelajaran ini dibuat, dari ekstrapolasi ke kasus tanpa noise, kita mendapat nilai ekspektasi 0.959. Nilaimu mungkin berbeda. Ini jauh lebih baik daripada nilai ekspektasi circuit mentah sebesar 0.83, sekitar 13% lebih dekat ke nilai ideal. Tapi kamu juga bisa melihat bahwa kita memakai satu titik data di mana nilai ekspektasinya turun sampai 0.31. Jelas titik data ini kualitasnya lebih buruk. Kalau titik data itu diberi bobot lebih rendah dalam aproksimasi linear kita, dan garisnya di-fit lebih ke dua titik data pertama, kita bisa melihat estimasi hasil ekstrapolasi ke nol akan lebih tinggi (lebih dekat ke nilai ideal). Pertimbangan semacam ini ditangani secara otomatis di ZNE bawaan Estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE built into Estimator {#zne-built-into-estimator}"
msgstr "ZNE bawaan Estimator {#zne-built-into-estimator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's see what happens when we use the ZNE functionality built into Estimator. We start by defining a simple GHZ circuit, without any gate folding.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita lihat apa yang terjadi ketika kita memakai fungsionalitas ZNE bawaan Estimator. Kita mulai dengan mendefinisikan circuit GHZ sederhana, tanpa gate folding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We define the same observable as before.\n"
msgstr "Kita mendefinisikan observable yang sama seperti sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We once again define a pass manager, using `optimization_level = 1`. We will return to this choice below.\n"
msgstr "Kita sekali lagi mendefinisikan pass manager, dengan `optimization_level = 1`. Kita akan kembali membahas pilihan ini di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit and apply the layout to the observables.\n"
msgstr "Transpile circuit dan terapkan layout ke observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We run the Estimator using ZNE and twirling, and we compare the outcomes to our ZNE by-hand implementation. In particular, we compare them to the result without ZNE (`value_no_zne`).\n"
msgstr "Kita menjalankan Estimator dengan ZNE dan twirling, lalu membandingkan hasilnya dengan implementasi ZNE manual kita. Secara khusus, kita bandingkan dengan hasil tanpa ZNE (`value_no_zne`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can retrieve the values at each noise factor using the syntax `job_zne.result()[0].data.evs_noise_factors`. As before, we could naively use these results to get a linear fit and extrapolate to the zero-noise case, but the estimator with `resilience_level = 2` has already done a better job, taking variance and other considerations into account. Below we show what a linear extrapolation would yield, and we show what built-in ZNE actually yielded.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa mengambil nilai pada tiap faktor noise dengan sintaks `job_zne.result()[0].data.evs_noise_factors`. Seperti sebelumnya, kita bisa saja memakai hasil ini secara naif untuk mendapat fit linear dan mengekstrapolasi ke kasus tanpa noise, tapi estimator dengan `resilience_level = 2` sudah bekerja lebih baik, dengan memperhitungkan varians dan pertimbangan lain. Di bawah kita tunjukkan apa yang akan dihasilkan ekstrapolasi linear, dan apa yang sebenarnya dihasilkan ZNE bawaan.\n"

