msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d54a12ec-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that the built-in ZNE improved our estimate by over 15%, and worked quite a bit better than our attempt by hand.\n"
msgstr "Kita lihat bahwa ZNE bawaan memperbaiki estimasi kita lebih dari 15%, dan bekerja jauh lebih baik daripada upaya manual kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving on, note that throughout this ZNE exploration, we have set `optimization_level = 1` in the pass manager. Higher levels of optimization reduce error, and sometimes the error reduction can make the errors scale less predictably. As is often the case, there is a balance: reduce errors, except when you are intentionally increasing them by a known factor.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum lanjut, perhatikan bahwa selama eksplorasi ZNE ini, kita mengatur `optimization_level = 1` di pass manager. Tingkat optimisasi yang lebih tinggi mengurangi error, dan kadang pengurangan error itu bisa membuat error berskala kurang bisa diprediksi. Seperti biasa, ada keseimbangan: kurangi error, kecuali saat kamu sengaja menaikkannya dengan faktor yang diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining methods {#combining-methods}"
msgstr "Menggabungkan metode {#combining-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE relies on the following:\n"
msgstr "ZNE bergantung pada hal-hal berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A well-defined noise-scaling parameter $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Parameter penskalaan noise $\\lambda$ yang terdefinisi dengan baik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sufficiently smooth and predictable scaling of expectation values with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan nilai ekspektasi terhadap $\\lambda$ yang cukup mulus dan bisa diprediksi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same effective noise channel, at different strengths\n"
msgstr "Noise channel efektif yang sama, pada kekuatan berbeda\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "No bias introduced that does not scale with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Tidak ada bias yang diperkenalkan yang tidak berskala dengan $\\lambda$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE combines cleanly with techniques that remove non-scaling biases (like M3) or make noise more regular (like twirling), but conflicts with techniques that either attempt to cancel noise entirely (PEC) or reshape it dynamically (DD).\n"
msgstr "ZNE bisa digabung dengan mulus bersama teknik yang menghilangkan bias non-skala (seperti M3) atau membuat noise lebih teratur (seperti twirling), tapi bertentangan dengan teknik yang berusaha membatalkan noise sepenuhnya (PEC) atau membentuk ulang noise secara dinamis (DD).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, M3 addresses only measurement/readout error, which in practice can be treated as separate from gate errors (which are the focus of error scaling processes in ZNE). M3 is largely independent of gate folding; it can be cleanly combined with ZNE. TREX is very similar, and it can be combined with ZNE.\n"
msgstr "Secara khusus, M3 hanya menangani error pengukuran/readout, yang dalam praktiknya bisa dianggap terpisah dari error gate (yang menjadi fokus proses penskalaan error di ZNE). M3 sebagian besar independen dari gate folding; M3 bisa digabung dengan ZNE secara bersih. TREX sangat mirip, dan bisa digabung dengan ZNE.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling does focus on gates, unlike M3 and TREX. However, recall that Pauli twirling does not directly mitigate error/noise; rather, it changes it to make it more predictable. Pauli twirling might actually be beneficial to the ZNE process in making gate errors scale more linearly and thus make the extrapolation more accurate.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling memang berfokus pada gate, tidak seperti M3 dan TREX. Namun, ingat bahwa Pauli twirling tidak memitigasi error/noise secara langsung; melainkan mengubahnya agar lebih mudah diprediksi. Pauli twirling bisa jadi malah menguntungkan proses ZNE karena membuat error gate berskala lebih linear sehingga ekstrapolasi lebih akurat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dynamical decoupling (DD) is more nuanced. DD dynamically alters noise behavior by partially cancelling certain errors through the addition of gate sequences. If it is possible to construct circuits in such a way that DD behaves the same even when gates or blocks are folded, then in principle one could combine ZNE and DD, but in practice DD sometimes interferes with the scaling. If you want to combine them, things to consider include the following:\n"
"* Is DD applied consistently at all noise levels?\n"
"* Does folding preserve the DD structure?\n"
"* Does the resulting noise scaling still behave monotonically?\n"
msgstr ""
"Dynamical decoupling (DD) lebih bernuansa. DD secara dinamis mengubah perilaku noise dengan membatalkan sebagian error tertentu lewat penambahan urutan gate. Kalau circuit bisa dibangun sedemikian rupa sehingga DD berperilaku sama bahkan ketika gate atau blok di-fold, maka secara prinsip kita bisa menggabungkan ZNE dan DD, tapi dalam praktiknya DD kadang mengganggu penskalaan. Kalau kamu ingin menggabungkannya, hal yang perlu dipertimbangkan antara lain:\n"
"* Apakah DD diterapkan secara konsisten di semua tingkat noise?\n"
"* Apakah folding mempertahankan struktur DD?\n"
"* Apakah penskalaan noise yang dihasilkan masih berperilaku monotonik?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last error mitigation method we will discuss as a standalone approach is not compatible with ZNE: probabilistic error cancellation.\n"
msgstr "Metode error mitigation terakhir yang akan kita bahas sebagai pendekatan mandiri tidak kompatibel dengan ZNE: probabilistic error cancellation.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"
msgstr "Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike ZNE or measurement mitigation, PEC attempts to cancel noise at the gate level by reconstructing the ideal channel in expectation. Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) is the most powerful and most expensive error-mitigation technique covered in this lesson. PEC is built around explicit inversion of the noise channel, carried out statistically rather than physically. PEC works by:\n"
msgstr "Tidak seperti ZNE atau mitigasi pengukuran, PEC berusaha membatalkan noise pada level gate dengan merekonstruksi channel ideal secara ekspektasi. Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) adalah teknik error-mitigation yang paling kuat sekaligus paling mahal yang dibahas di pelajaran ini. PEC dibangun di sekitar inversi eksplisit dari noise channel, yang dilakukan secara statistik, bukan secara fisik. PEC bekerja dengan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise model in terms of a basis of \"error operations.\"\n"
msgstr "Mengkarakterisasi model noise dalam basis \"operasi error.\"\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressing the inverse of the noise channel as a quasi-probability distribution over physical operations.\n"
msgstr "Menyatakan invers dari noise channel sebagai distribusi quasi-probability atas operasi fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling from this distribution during circuit execution to statistically construct an unbiased estimate of the ideal computation.\n"
msgstr "Melakukan sampling dari distribusi ini selama eksekusi circuit untuk membangun secara statistik estimasi tak bias dari komputasi ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptually, PEC is like virtual error correction &mdash; it \"undoes\" noise by combining noisy operations in carefully weighted random patterns. Procedurally, however, PEC is not closely related to error correction or detection code. PEC's unbiased estimation of the ideal, noiseless expectation value comes at the cost of a very large sampling overhead and a strong dependence on accurate noise characterization.\n"
msgstr "Secara konseptual, PEC seperti koreksi error virtual &mdash; PEC \"membatalkan\" noise dengan menggabungkan operasi bernoise dalam pola acak yang bobotnya diatur dengan cermat. Namun secara prosedur, PEC tidak terkait erat dengan error correction atau kode deteksi error. Estimasi tak bias PEC terhadap nilai ekspektasi ideal tanpa noise datang dengan harga overhead sampling yang sangat besar dan ketergantungan kuat pada karakterisasi noise yang akurat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On IBM quantum computers, PEC is best viewed as a precision tool rather than a general-purpose mitigation layer: it is most appropriate for small circuits or small portions of larger circuits, benchmarking tasks, and high-accuracy studies where high quantum overhead is acceptable.\n"
msgstr "Di komputer kuantum IBM, PEC paling tepat dipandang sebagai alat presisi, bukan lapisan mitigasi serba guna: PEC paling cocok untuk circuit kecil atau bagian kecil dari circuit yang lebih besar, tugas benchmarking, dan studi berakurasi tinggi di mana overhead kuantum yang tinggi bisa diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise channel {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Mengkarakterisasi noise channel {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In PEC, each ideal gate in a quantum circuit is modeled as an **ideal unitary channel** followed by a noise process. Let $\\rho$ denote the density matrix of the quantum state. The ideal gate is represented by a unitary matrix $U$, which induces a quantum channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Di PEC, setiap gate ideal dalam quantum circuit dimodelkan sebagai **unitary channel ideal** yang diikuti oleh proses noise. Misalkan $\\rho$ menyatakan density matrix dari quantum state. Gate ideal direpresentasikan oleh matriks unitary $U$, yang menginduksi quantum channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On real hardware, this ideal evolution is corrupted by noise. We model the physical implementation of the gate as an **effective noisy channel**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\mathcal{N}$ is a noise channel capturing the stochastic errors associated with the gate. Throughout this discussion, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, and $\\mathcal{E}$ are linear maps acting on density operators. The ideal channel $\\mathcal{U}$ is unitary and reversible, while the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ (and hence $\\mathcal{E}$) is a completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP) map.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada hardware sungguhan, evolusi ideal ini dirusak oleh noise. Kita memodelkan implementasi fisik dari gate sebagai **noisy channel efektif**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"dengan $\\mathcal{N}$ adalah noise channel yang menangkap error stokastik yang terkait dengan gate. Sepanjang pembahasan ini, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, dan $\\mathcal{E}$ adalah peta linear yang bekerja pada operator densitas. Channel ideal $\\mathcal{U}$ bersifat unitary dan reversibel, sedangkan noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ (dan karenanya $\\mathcal{E}$) adalah peta completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC assumes that the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ is known or approximately known. On IBM Quantum hardware, this information is typically obtained from device calibration data, error rates inferred from benchmarking experiments, and simplified noise models such as Pauli or depolarizing approximations for small gate sets. While PEC does not require a perfectly accurate noise model, its performance degrades rapidly as the assumed noise channel diverges from the true hardware behavior.\n"
msgstr "PEC mengasumsikan bahwa noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ diketahui atau kira-kira diketahui. Pada hardware IBM Quantum, informasi ini biasanya diperoleh dari data kalibrasi perangkat, laju error yang disimpulkan dari eksperimen benchmarking, dan model noise yang disederhanakan seperti aproksimasi Pauli atau depolarizing untuk set gate kecil. Meski PEC tidak membutuhkan model noise yang sempurna akurat, kinerjanya menurun dengan cepat ketika noise channel yang diasumsikan menyimpang dari perilaku hardware sebenarnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decomposition of the inverse noise channel {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Dekomposisi quasi-probability dari invers noise channel {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The central idea of PEC is to **cancel the effect of noise in expectation** by constructing a stochastic approximation to the inverse of the noise channel. Formally, the goal is to apply a linear map that approximately undoes $\\mathcal{N}$, such that:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"in expectation over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagasan utama PEC adalah **membatalkan efek noise secara ekspektasi** dengan membangun aproksimasi stokastik dari invers noise channel. Secara formal, tujuannya adalah menerapkan peta linear yang kira-kira membatalkan $\\mathcal{N}$, sehingga:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"secara ekspektasi atas banyak eksekusi circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The inverse $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ is defined here as the algebraic inverse of $\\mathcal{N}$ treated as a linear superoperator acting on operators. This inverse exists only if $\\mathcal{N}$ is full-rank; non-invertible noise processes cannot be exactly mitigated using PEC.\n"
msgstr "Invers $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ di sini didefinisikan sebagai invers aljabar dari $\\mathcal{N}$ yang diperlakukan sebagai superoperator linear yang bekerja pada operator. Invers ini ada hanya jika $\\mathcal{N}$ berperingkat penuh (full-rank); proses noise yang tidak bisa diinversi tidak dapat dimitigasi secara tepat dengan PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When inversion is possible, PEC expresses the inverse noise channel as a **linear combination of physically implementable operations**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Here, each $\\mathcal{O}_i$ is a noisy operation that can be executed on the hardware (typically native gates or short gate sequences), and the real coefficients $\\eta_i$ form a **quasi-probability distribution**. Unlike ordinary probabilities, the coefficients $\\eta_i$ might be negative or exceed 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika inversi memungkinkan, PEC menyatakan invers noise channel sebagai **kombinasi linear dari operasi yang bisa diimplementasikan secara fisik**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Di sini, setiap $\\mathcal{O}_i$ adalah operasi bernoise yang bisa dieksekusi di hardware (biasanya gate native atau urutan gate pendek), dan koefisien real $\\eta_i$ membentuk **distribusi quasi-probability**. Berbeda dengan probabilitas biasa, koefisien $\\eta_i$ bisa negatif atau melebihi 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **quasi-probability norm**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"quantifies the cost of the noise inversion. For any nontrivial noise channel, $\\gamma > 1$. On IBM Quantum hardware, this decomposition is typically performed:\n"
"- per gate or per small gate set,\n"
"- assuming restricted noise models (often Pauli-diagonal approximations),\n"
"- using backend-specific native operations and scheduling constraints.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Norma quasi-probability**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"mengukur biaya inversi noise. Untuk noise channel nontrivial apa pun, $\\gamma > 1$. Pada hardware IBM Quantum, dekomposisi ini biasanya dilakukan:\n"
"- per gate atau per set gate kecil,\n"
"- dengan mengasumsikan model noise terbatas (sering aproksimasi Pauli-diagonal),\n"
"- menggunakan operasi native spesifik backend dan batasan penjadwalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monte Carlo reconstruction of the ideal circuit {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"
msgstr "Rekonstruksi Monte Carlo dari circuit ideal {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To estimate the expectation value of an observable $O$, PEC uses Monte Carlo sampling based on the decomposition above. For each occurrence of a noisy gate in the circuit, the following procedure is applied:\n"
msgstr "Untuk memperkirakan nilai ekspektasi dari observable $O$, PEC memakai sampling Monte Carlo berdasarkan dekomposisi di atas. Untuk setiap kemunculan gate bernoise di circuit, prosedur berikut diterapkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Randomly select an operation $\\mathcal{O}_i$ with probability:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih secara acak sebuah operasi $\\mathcal{O}_i$ dengan probabilitas:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assign a classical weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tetapkan bobot klasik:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the resulting randomized noisy circuit on the quantum backend.\n"
msgstr "Eksekusi circuit bernoise acak yang dihasilkan di backend kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the measured outcome by the product of all accumulated weights.\n"
msgstr "Kalikan hasil pengukuran dengan hasil kali semua bobot yang terakumulasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Average the weighted results over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr "Rata-ratakan hasil berbobot itu atas banyak eksekusi circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The resulting estimator $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ satisfies\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"provided the noise model $\\mathcal{N}$ accurately describes the hardware. PEC therefore introduces **no systematic bias** in expectation, but replaces bias with **large statistical variance**. Each run produces a noisy but weighted estimate; only after averaging many such runs does the ideal expectation value emerge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estimator yang dihasilkan $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ memenuhi\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"asalkan model noise $\\mathcal{N}$ menggambarkan hardware dengan akurat. Jadi PEC memperkenalkan **tidak ada bias sistematis** secara ekspektasi, tapi menukar bias dengan **varians statistik yang besar**. Setiap run menghasilkan estimasi yang noisy tapi berbobot; hanya setelah merata-ratakan banyak run seperti itu nilai ekspektasi ideal muncul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual interpretation {#conceptual-interpretation}"
msgstr "Interpretasi konseptual {#conceptual-interpretation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is sometimes described as *virtual error correction*. While this phrasing is not entirely incorrect, it should not be confused with true quantum error correction. PEC involves no logical encoding, no syndrome extraction, and no real-time feedback. Errors are not prevented or corrected during circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "PEC kadang digambarkan sebagai *virtual error correction*. Meski pernyataan ini tidak sepenuhnya salah, jangan disamakan dengan quantum error correction yang sebenarnya. PEC tidak melibatkan logical encoding, tidak ada syndrome extraction, dan tidak ada umpan balik real-time. Error tidak dicegah atau dikoreksi selama eksekusi circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead, PEC cancels noise **statistically**, by combining many noisy circuit realizations with signed classical weights so that errors cancel only after classical post-processing. Information is not protected during execution; ideal results are reconstructed after the fact.\n"
msgstr "Sebaliknya, PEC membatalkan noise **secara statistik**, dengan menggabungkan banyak realisasi circuit bernoise dengan bobot klasik bertanda sehingga error saling membatalkan hanya setelah post-processing klasik. Informasi tidak dilindungi selama eksekusi; hasil ideal direkonstruksi setelah kejadian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resource scaling and cost {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"
msgstr "Penskalaan resource dan biaya {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dominant cost of PEC stems from variance amplification. The variance of the PEC estimator scales as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"implying:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Required number of shots} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Biaya dominan PEC berasal dari penguatan varians. Varians estimator PEC berskala sebagai:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"yang menyiratkan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Jumlah shot yang dibutuhkan} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This scaling is fundamental and cannot be improved through classical post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan ini bersifat fundamental dan tidak bisa diperbaiki lewat post-processing klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For circuits containing many noisy gates, each gate contributes a factor $\\gamma_k > 1$, causing the total quasi-probability norm to grow approximately multiplicatively:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d$ is the circuit depth. On IBM Quantum hardware, this typically leads to exponential growth in sampling cost with circuit depth, with particularly strong sensitivity to two-qubit gate errors. This scaling places practical limits on the applicability of PEC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk circuit yang berisi banyak gate bernoise, setiap gate menyumbang faktor $\\gamma_k > 1$, sehingga norma quasi-probability total tumbuh kira-kira secara perkalian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"dengan $d$ adalah depth circuit. Pada hardware IBM Quantum, ini biasanya menyebabkan pertumbuhan eksponensial biaya sampling terhadap depth circuit, dengan sensitivitas yang sangat kuat terhadap error gate dua-qubit. Penskalaan ini membatasi penerapan PEC secara praktis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is currently practical only when one or all of the following conditions are met:\n"
msgstr "PEC saat ini praktis hanya ketika satu atau semua kondisi berikut terpenuhi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuits are very small or shallow (often $\\leq 10-20$ gates),\n"
msgstr "Circuit sangat kecil atau dangkal (sering $\\leq 10-20$ gate),\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise models are simple and well-validated (for example, Pauli noise),\n"
msgstr "Model noise sederhana dan tervalidasi dengan baik (misalnya noise Pauli),\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High statistical cost is acceptable,\n"
msgstr "Biaya statistik yang tinggi bisa diterima,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The goal is accuracy rather than throughput.\n"
msgstr "Tujuannya adalah akurasi, bukan throughput.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this reason, PEC is often applied to:\n"
msgstr "Karena itu, PEC sering diterapkan pada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Isolated subcircuits within larger workflows,\n"
msgstr "Subcircuit terisolasi di dalam workflow yang lebih besar,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short-time evolution steps,\n"
msgstr "Langkah evolusi waktu singkat,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "State preparation or measurement routines,\n"
msgstr "Rutinitas persiapan state atau pengukuran,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarking and validation experiments.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen benchmarking dan validasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IBM software stack (IBM Quantum Compute and error-mitigation tooling) reflects this by treating PEC as a specialized option, not a default mitigation layer.\n"
msgstr "Software stack IBM (IBM Quantum Compute dan tooling error-mitigation) mencerminkan hal ini dengan memperlakukan PEC sebagai opsi khusus, bukan lapisan mitigasi default.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical PEC use cases include:\n"
msgstr "Contoh kasus penggunaan PEC yang umum meliputi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Precision benchmarking of quantum hardware,\n"
msgstr "Benchmarking presisi untuk hardware kuantum,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification of small quantum algorithms,\n"
msgstr "Verifikasi algoritma kuantum kecil,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-accuracy quantum chemistry on reduced systems,\n"
msgstr "Kimia kuantum dengan akurasi tinggi pada sistem yang direduksi,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-checking ZNE or other mitigation methods.\n"
msgstr "Pengecekan silang ZNE atau metode mitigasi lainnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC's relationship to other mitigation methods {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"
msgstr "Hubungan PEC dengan metode mitigasi lainnya {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many other mitigation techniques trade accuracy for scalability; PEC does just the opposite, focusing on accuracy above all else.\n"
msgstr "Banyak teknik mitigasi lain mengorbankan akurasi demi skalabilitas; PEC justru kebalikannya, yaitu mengutamakan akurasi di atas segalanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because PEC might only be used on a subcircuit, it is especially important here to ask what other mitigation methods can be combined with it. To reason clearly about compatibility with PEC, it helps to categorize techniques by what they do to the noise. Consider these general categories:\n"
msgstr "Karena PEC mungkin hanya dipakai pada sebuah subcircuit, di sini penting sekali untuk bertanya metode mitigasi lain apa yang bisa dikombinasikan dengannya. Untuk menalar kompatibilitas dengan PEC secara jelas, ada baiknya mengelompokkan teknik berdasarkan apa yang mereka lakukan terhadap noise. Perhatikan kategori umum berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise cancellation - attempt to invert error channels\n"
msgstr "Pembatalan noise - berusaha membalik error channel\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise scaling - deliberately increase noise to extrapolate\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan noise - sengaja menaikkan noise untuk ekstrapolasi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise reshaping - change the structure or spectrum of noise\n"
msgstr "Pembentukan ulang noise - mengubah struktur atau spektrum noise\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bias removal - correct errors that do not scale with gate noise\n"
msgstr "Penghapusan bias - mengoreksi error yang tidak berskala dengan noise Gate\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC sits squarely in category (1). Any method that changes or rescales the noise channel must be examined carefully.\n"
msgstr "PEC jelas berada di kategori (1). Metode apa pun yang mengubah atau menskalakan ulang noise channel harus diperiksa dengan hati-hati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary table (high-level)\n"
msgstr "Tabel ringkasan (tingkat tinggi)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Technique | Compatible with PEC | Notes |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | No | Undoing versus scaling and sometimes tailoring error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Yes (with care) | Affects error behavior, but might make it easier to learn |\n"
"| TREX | Yes | No overlap in workflow. Fully compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Usually no | Changes error channel |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Teknik | Kompatibel dengan PEC | Catatan |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | Tidak | Membatalkan versus menskalakan, dan kadang menyesuaikan error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Ya (dengan hati-hati) | Memengaruhi perilaku error, tetapi mungkin membuatnya lebih mudah dipelajari |\n"
"| TREX | Ya | Tidak ada tumpang tindih dalam alur kerja. Sepenuhnya kompatibel. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Biasanya tidak | Mengubah error channel |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and ZNE address the same error sources (gate errors) via mutually incompatible assumptions or workstreams, or both. For example, in ZNE, we assume error can be expanded in a parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"and that the error can be effectively scaled to model this expansion. PEC would undo the very error we rely on for the scaling. The parameter $\\lambda$ would become meaningless. Another way of thinking about it is:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC dan ZNE menangani sumber error yang sama (error Gate) lewat asumsi atau alur kerja yang saling tidak kompatibel, atau keduanya. Misalnya, pada ZNE kita berasumsi error bisa diekspansi dalam parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"dan error tersebut bisa diskalakan secara efektif untuk memodelkan ekspansi ini. PEC akan membatalkan error yang justru kita andalkan untuk penskalaan. Parameter $\\lambda$ jadi tidak bermakna. Cara lain memikirkannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying ZNE before PEC changes the noise channel you are trying to invert.\n"
msgstr "Menerapkan ZNE sebelum PEC mengubah noise channel yang mau Anda balik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC before ZNE removes the very noise ZNE relies on to extrapolate.\n"
msgstr "Menerapkan PEC sebelum ZNE menghilangkan noise yang diandalkan ZNE untuk ekstrapolasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC and ZNE should be considered alternative error-mitigation paradigms, not composable layers. Comparing them side-by-side is instructive, while combining them is not.\n"
msgstr "PEC dan ZNE sebaiknya dianggap sebagai paradigma mitigasi error alternatif, bukan lapisan yang bisa digabungkan. Membandingkan keduanya secara berdampingan itu bermanfaat, sedangkan menggabungkannya tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and Pauli twirling are generally compatible and often beneficial.\n"
"Twirling might help PEC in that twirling converts coherent errors into stochastic Pauli errors. This simplifies the noise channel, making it easier to represent and invert. For PEC, this is extremely valuable, for the following reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC dan Pauli twirling umumnya kompatibel dan sering menguntungkan.\n"
"Twirling bisa membantu PEC karena twirling mengubah error koheren menjadi error Pauli stokastik. Ini menyederhanakan noise channel sehingga lebih mudah direpresentasikan dan dibalik. Bagi PEC, ini sangat berharga karena alasan berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decompositions are much simpler for Pauli channels\n"
msgstr "Dekomposisi quasi-probability jauh lebih sederhana untuk Pauli channel\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quasi-probability norm $\\gamma$ is often significantly smaller\n"
msgstr "Norma quasi-probability $\\gamma$ sering kali jauh lebih kecil\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling variance is reduced\n"
msgstr "Varians sampling berkurang\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many PEC demonstrations assume or build in Pauli-twirled noise.\n"
"It's important to clarify that Pauli twirling does not mitigate errors by itself; it reshapes noise into a form that probabilistic error cancellation can handle more efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Banyak demonstrasi PEC mengasumsikan atau membangun noise yang sudah di-Pauli-twirl.\n"
"Penting untuk ditegaskan bahwa Pauli twirling tidak memitigasi error dengan sendirinya; ia membentuk ulang noise ke bentuk yang bisa ditangani probabilistic error cancellation dengan lebih efisien.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC can and should be combined with TREX. These approaches are fully compatible and play orthogonal roles. TREX operates only at measurement, removes readout bias via randomized twirls of the measurement channel, and does not affect gate noise or circuit dynamics. PEC operates on gate noise. Because measurement error is additive rather than compositional, it is independent of gate sequences. It is safe and often desirable to apply TREX alongside PEC.\n"
msgstr "PEC bisa dan sebaiknya dikombinasikan dengan TREX. Kedua pendekatan ini sepenuhnya kompatibel dan berperan secara ortogonal. TREX hanya bekerja pada pengukuran, menghilangkan bias readout lewat twirl acak pada measurement channel, dan tidak memengaruhi noise Gate maupun dinamika Circuit. PEC bekerja pada noise Gate. Karena error pengukuran bersifat aditif, bukan komposisional, ia tidak bergantung pada urutan Gate. Aman dan sering diinginkan untuk menerapkan TREX bersama PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering of these methods is what you might expect:\n"
"1. Execute PEC-randomized circuit\n"
"2. Apply TREX to mitigate readout error\n"
"3. Apply PEC weighting and averaging\n"
msgstr ""
"Urutan metode-metode ini sesuai dugaan Anda:\n"
"1. Jalankan Circuit PEC yang diacak\n"
"2. Terapkan TREX untuk memitigasi error readout\n"
"3. Terapkan pembobotan dan perataan PEC\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and DD are generally incompatible unless the noise characterization used for PEC is performed with DD active. PEC assumes that $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"is stationary, repeatable, and accurately characterizable. DD explicitly reshapes the noise channel in time by modulating system-environment interactions and introducing non-trivial pulse-timing effects. As a result, the effective noise with DD is not the same channel as without DD. This is made even more complex by the fact that the noise channel can depend sensitively on circuit scheduling. The end result is that noise inversion becomes ill-defined or invalid.\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC dan DD umumnya tidak kompatibel kecuali karakterisasi noise yang dipakai untuk PEC dilakukan dengan DD aktif. PEC mengasumsikan bahwa $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"bersifat stasioner, dapat diulang, dan dapat dikarakterisasi dengan akurat. DD secara eksplisit membentuk ulang noise channel dalam waktu dengan memodulasi interaksi sistem-lingkungan dan memunculkan efek pewaktuan pulsa yang tidak sepele. Akibatnya, noise efektif dengan DD bukan channel yang sama dengan tanpa DD. Ini makin rumit karena noise channel bisa sangat bergantung pada penjadwalan Circuit. Hasil akhirnya, pembalikan noise menjadi tidak terdefinisi dengan baik atau tidak valid.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is theoretically possible to characterize noise with DD active and build a PEC model accordingly, but this is highly advanced and not currently a recommended workflow.\n"
msgstr "Secara teori, memang mungkin mengkarakterisasi noise dengan DD aktif lalu membangun model PEC yang sesuai, tetapi ini sangat tingkat lanjut dan saat ini bukan alur kerja yang direkomendasikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC by hand {#applying-pec-by-hand}"
msgstr "Menerapkan PEC secara manual {#applying-pec-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is complex and it is not recommended that you implement it by hand. Still, we want to work through the math of a basic application on a single qubit to understand what steps the process entails. We choose a mixed but nontrivial state so that we can see numerical effects clearly.\n"
msgstr "PEC itu kompleks dan tidak disarankan untuk diimplementasikan secara manual. Meski begitu, kita ingin menelusuri matematika dari penerapan dasar pada satu qubit untuk memahami langkah apa saja yang terlibat. Kita memilih state campuran yang tidak sepele supaya efek numeriknya terlihat jelas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Take a qubit that should be in the pure state\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ambil sebuah qubit yang seharusnya berada di pure state\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ideal density matrix is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks densitas idealnya adalah:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"We've chosen this density matrix because it is not diagonal and is only for a single qubit so that it is tractable to examine \"by hand\".\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Kita memilih matriks densitas ini karena tidak diagonal dan hanya untuk satu qubit, sehingga mudah diperiksa \"secara manual\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now apply a very simple, but realistic noise model: a single-qubit depolarizing channel, with small strength $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita terapkan model noise yang sangat sederhana tetapi realistis: depolarizing channel satu qubit dengan kekuatan kecil $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep the arithmetic friendly, take $p = 0.15$. This channel is completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP), as it must be. It is a realistic noise channel for real hardware, or at least realistic for describing some of the noise. Further, this noise channel is analytically invertible, as a linear map. In other words, there exists an inverse matrix, but that doesn't mean that the matrix corresponds to a CPTP physical channel, and it certainly doesn't correspond to a unitary that could be implemented on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Supaya hitungannya mudah, ambil $p = 0.15$. Channel ini completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP), sebagaimana mestinya. Channel ini realistis untuk hardware nyata, atau setidaknya realistis untuk menggambarkan sebagian noise. Lebih jauh, noise channel ini dapat dibalik secara analitis sebagai pemetaan linear. Dengan kata lain, ada matriks inversnya, tetapi itu tidak berarti matriks tersebut sesuai dengan channel fisik CPTP, dan jelas tidak sesuai dengan unitary yang bisa diimplementasikan di hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we apply our depolarizing noise channel to our single-qubit density matrix and obtain:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"With $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ and $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita terapkan depolarizing noise channel ke matriks densitas satu qubit kita dan diperoleh:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"Dengan $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ dan $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying this to our state:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Menerapkannya pada state kita:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute explicitly:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung secara eksplisit:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"This is still a physical density matrix, and it still has trace one &mdash; but it is more mixed now.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(dibulatkan)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Ini masih matriks densitas fisik, dan trace-nya masih satu &mdash; tetapi sekarang lebih tercampur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we compute the ideal inverse channel, but being very prepared for the possibility that it might not be physical. We will check whether it is. Mathematically, the inverse linear map is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita hitung inverse channel yang ideal, tetapi dengan kesiapan penuh bahwa ia mungkin tidak fisik. Kita akan memeriksa apakah ia fisik. Secara matematis, pemetaan linear inversnya adalah:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If this inverse action were itself a valid physical channel, then we would be tempted to try to implement it exactly. Of course, we would still need to figure out how to implement it using unitary operations and classical steps, but implementing this would be the goal. However, it turns out this is *not* CPTP, and there is generally no guarantee that such inverse mappings will be CPTP. That is critical to our current discussion, because it is the reason PEC exists.\n"
msgstr "Jika aksi invers ini sendiri merupakan channel fisik yang valid, kita akan tergoda untuk mengimplementasikannya secara persis. Tentu kita masih harus mencari cara mengimplementasikannya dengan operasi unitary dan langkah klasik, tetapi itulah tujuannya. Namun, ternyata ini *bukan* CPTP, dan secara umum tidak ada jaminan bahwa pemetaan invers seperti itu CPTP. Hal itu penting untuk pembahasan kita sekarang, karena itulah alasan PEC ada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might be able to see that it is not CPTP just by looking at it. A sure-fire check is to apply it to a density matrix and see if it returns physical results. This is left as an exercise to check your understanding.\n"
msgstr "Anda mungkin bisa melihat bahwa ini bukan CPTP hanya dengan memandanginya. Cara pengecekan yang pasti adalah menerapkannya pada sebuah matriks densitas dan melihat apakah hasilnya fisik. Ini dijadikan latihan untuk menguji pemahaman Anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Uji pemahaman Anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether the inverse mapping from above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ is CPTP by applying it to a new density matrix:\n"
msgstr "Periksa apakah pemetaan invers $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ di atas CPTP dengan menerapkannya pada matriks densitas baru:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results as being physical or non-physical.\n"
msgstr "Tafsirkan hasilnya sebagai fisik atau non-fisik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a physical density matrix, this corresponds to a classical probability of greater than 1 that the system is in the state $|0\\rangle$ and a negative probability of being in the state $|1\\rangle$. Clearly this mapping can yield nonsense density matrices. Further, by inspection we can see that the eigenvalues of the resulting density matrix are 1.0625 and -0.0625, meaning not all eigenvalues are positive. Thus the mapping is not \"completely positive\", the \"CP\" in CPTP.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai matriks densitas fisik, ini berarti probabilitas klasik lebih dari 1 bahwa sistem berada di state $|0\\rangle$ dan probabilitas negatif berada di state $|1\\rangle$. Jelas pemetaan ini bisa menghasilkan matriks densitas yang tidak masuk akal. Selain itu, dengan inspeksi kita bisa melihat bahwa nilai eigen dari matriks densitas hasilnya adalah 1.0625 dan -0.0625, artinya tidak semua nilai eigen positif. Jadi pemetaan ini tidak \"completely positive\", yaitu \"CP\" dalam CPTP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check by explicit calculation that the inverse operation above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ undoes the noise channel and returns the noise-free state.\n"
msgstr "Periksa lewat perhitungan eksplisit bahwa operasi invers $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ di atas membatalkan noise channel dan mengembalikan state bebas noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it to the noisy state:\n"
msgstr "Terapkan pada state yang berisik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is exactly the original state (up to rounding).\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Ini persis state aslinya (sampai pembulatan).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We restate to be absolutely clear: we cannot invert the noise channel exactly; the inverse is not CPTP, nor is it a valid physical channel. However, we can effectively invert the channel as a linear combination of physical channels.\n"
msgstr "Kita ulangi agar benar-benar jelas: kita tidak bisa membalik noise channel secara persis; inversnya bukan CPTP, dan juga bukan channel fisik yang valid. Namun, kita bisa membalik channel tersebut secara efektif sebagai kombinasi linear dari channel-channel fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"where: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"dengan: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ dan seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The inverse can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Inversnya dapat ditulis sebagai:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with:\n"
msgstr "with:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = physically implementable Clifford channels\n"
msgstr "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = Clifford channel yang bisa diimplementasikan secara fisik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilities\n"
msgstr "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probability\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "Inilah ide inti di balik PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Sampling channel sesuai $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Lampirkan tanda pada hasil pengukuran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Nilai ekspektasi konvergen ke nilai bebas noise\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Kita terapkan PEC \"secara manual\" untuk mengestimasi $\\langle Z \\rangle$ dengan memakai matriks densitas $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ dan melihat apakah kita bisa memulihkan hasil untuk $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Untuk $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ kita mengharapkan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan juga bahwa untuk matriks densitas yang berisik, kita peroleh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "Orde besarnya sudah benar tetapi masih cukup jauh dari kasus ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita telusuri bagaimana, dengan proses PEC, kita bisa merekonstruksi nilai ekspektasi tak bias dari matriks densitas yang berisik. Dalam alur kerja nyata, ini bersifat probabilistik dan akan diotomatisasi. Dalam alur kerja \"manual\" ini, kita akan memilih nilai probabilistik yang realistis, tetapi mungkin nyaman untuk presentasi kita. Ini tidak boleh dianggap sebagai klaim bahwa PEC sempurna. Ini hanya untuk menunjukkan skenario masuk akal yang bisa terjadi di dalam paket PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa noise channel kita berbentuk:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"Inversnya dapat ditulis (persis):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Untuk pengantar ini lebih sederhana jika kita fokus pada efek channel terhadap matriks densitas kita. Ini memungkinkan kita bekerja dengan objek yang familier seperti matriks densitas dan nilai ekspektasi. Untuk itu, pertimbangkan apa yang harus benar tentang efek operasi invers ini pada proses estimasi kita: estimator yang dihasilkan PEC harus ternormalisasi dan tak bias. Ini berkaitan dengan dua kondisi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalisasi: Agar operasi ini tidak mengubah skala observable, kita membutuhkan $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Untuk melihat kenapa begitu, kita bisa meninjau aksi invers pada matriks densitas, atau meninjau aksinya pada nilai ekspektasi sesuatu yang sepele seperti $\\mathcal{I}$ itu sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Kalibrasi: Dalam alur kerja nyata, kita memakai Circuit kalibrasi untuk mempelajari perilaku noise pada level Gate. Kita lalu memakai pengetahuan perilaku noise level Gate itu, dan linearitas nilai ekspektasi, untuk menerapkan model noise yang dipelajari ke Circuit yang lebih besar. Dalam kasus kita, kita mulai dengan pengetahuan buatan bahwa nilai ekspektasi idealnya $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Tetapi sangat mudah membuat state yang secara teori kita tahu bahwa itu nilai idealnya, lalu memakai pengukuran nyata untuk kalibrasi. Poin kuncinya, untuk PEC biasanya kita tidak mempelajari model noise lengkap dari seluruh Circuit. Sebaliknya, kita mempelajari model noise lokal untuk Gate individual atau lapisan Circuit dan memakainya untuk membangun dekomposisi quasi-probability.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Kita memakai kondisi-kondisi ini untuk menentukan $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$. Kita pertimbangkan ansatz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa Pauli channel bekerja lewat konjugasi:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Menerapkan $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ pada $\\rho$ menghasilkan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengambil trace, kita peroleh:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap operator Pauli bersifat unitary, sehingga konjugasi mempertahankan trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Agar estimator PEC ternormalisasi, pemetaan invers efektif\n"
"harus mempertahankan trace dari semua matriks densitas. Artinya, kita membutuhkan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini menyiratkan batasan normalisasi:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "Tetapi dalam kasus kita, ini menghasilkan kondisi:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita memakai informasi kalibrasi untuk menghubungkan nilai ekspektasi yang teramati dengan nilai ideal yang diketahui.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving our two conditions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Dengan menyelesaikan kedua kondisi kita untuk $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$, kita peroleh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These coefficients sum to 1, but one of them is negative.\n"
msgstr "Koefisien-koefisien ini berjumlah 1, tetapi salah satunya negatif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can recover the ideal expectation value by randomly modifying the circuit, measuring, multiplying the result by a signed weight, and averaging. In particular, no density matrices are reconstructed and no inverse channel is implemented physically.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa memulihkan nilai ekspektasi ideal dengan memodifikasi Circuit secara acak, mengukur, mengalikan hasilnya dengan bobot bertanda, lalu merata-ratakan. Perlu dicatat, tidak ada matriks densitas yang direkonstruksi dan tidak ada inverse channel yang diimplementasikan secara fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key step: this is PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"
msgstr "Langkah kuncinya: inilah PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our noise strength $p=0.15$, the inverse channel can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kekuatan noise kita $p=0.15$, inverse channel dapat ditulis sebagai:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important facts:\n"
msgstr "Fakta penting:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients sum to 1\n"
msgstr "Koefisien-koefisiennya berjumlah 1\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "One coefficient is negative\n"
msgstr "Satu koefisien bernilai negatif\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each term is physically implementable\n"
msgstr "Setiap suku dapat diimplementasikan secara fisik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The negativity moves into classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "Negativitasnya dipindahkan ke pasca-pemrosesan klasik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We form a sampling distribution from the absolute values of the weights:\n"
msgstr "Kita membentuk distribusi sampling dari nilai absolut bobot:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(for each of X, Y, Z)\n"
msgstr "(untuk masing-masing X, Y, Z)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Total weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Bobot total:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For sampling probabilities, divide by W.\n"
msgstr "Untuk probabilitas sampling, bagi dengan W.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Operation | Probability | Sign |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Do nothing ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Apply X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Operasi | Probabilitas | Tanda |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Tidak melakukan apa-apa ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Terapkan X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Terapkan Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Terapkan Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sign comes from the original coefficient, not the probability.\n"
msgstr "Tanda berasal dari koefisien aslinya, bukan dari probabilitas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each shot consists of these steps:\n"
msgstr "Setiap shot terdiri dari langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the state\n"
msgstr "Siapkan state\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the hardware apply the noisy circuit\n"
msgstr "Biarkan hardware menerapkan Circuit yang berisik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomly choose an operation from the table above using the associated probabilities\n"
msgstr "Pilih operasi secara acak dari tabel di atas menggunakan probabilitas yang terkait\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
